1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,448
Ninety-five percent of people use AI

2
00:00:02,448 --> 00:00:04,149
like a faster typewriter.

3
00:00:04,149 --> 00:00:06,121
They sit inside a chat window

4
00:00:06,121 --> 00:00:08,774
all afternoon trading manual typing for

5
00:00:08,774 --> 00:00:09,930
manual prompting.

6
00:00:09,930 --> 00:00:10,504
In 1913,

7
00:00:10,504 --> 00:00:12,872
Henry Ford did not hand mechanics

8
00:00:12,872 --> 00:00:15,240
faster wrenches - he engineered a

9
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:17,034
repeatable assembly line.

10
00:00:17,034 --> 00:00:17,465
Today,

11
00:00:17,465 --> 00:00:19,976
solo operators face that exact same

12
00:00:19,976 --> 00:00:21,770
divide with digital work.

13
00:00:21,770 --> 00:00:23,760
Chatting one prompt at a time

14
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:26,230
keeps you trapped as the bottleneck.

15
00:00:26,230 --> 00:00:28,974
Building a workflow turns one documented

16
00:00:28,974 --> 00:00:31,993
standard operating procedure into a pipeline

17
00:00:31,993 --> 00:00:33,640
that runs on raw inputs.

18
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:35,527
Apply the Three-Block Rule:

19
00:00:35,527 --> 00:00:37,903
whenever you repeat a digital task

20
00:00:37,903 --> 00:00:38,742
three times,

21
00:00:38,742 --> 00:00:40,909
stop chatting and write a fixed

22
00:00:40,909 --> 00:00:42,726
spec - exact input format,

23
00:00:42,726 --> 00:00:44,473
strict quality checklist,

24
00:00:44,473 --> 00:00:46,500
and a locked output template.

25
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:49,686
Amateurs write clever prompts from scratch;

26
00:00:49,686 --> 00:00:52,428
owners design pipelines once and feed

27
00:00:52,428 --> 00:00:53,539
them raw ideas.

28
00:00:53,539 --> 00:00:55,910
And until you make that shift...
